-- title:
--   Transversal crossing: branch ideals sum to the maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$, and assume $j$, given as the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ`, lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho \colon R_p \to A$ a ring map inducing the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O \colon R_p \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, together with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa_A$ satisfying $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{res}_A \circ \rho$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two maps $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ 0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ 1$ (the two components of the geometric special fibre), and let $x_n$ be the induced point of $X_O = X \times_{R_p} \operatorname{Spec} O$ obtained by composing the first projection, $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ 0$ and the base-change map `bcMap`. Assume the two points $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$ of $X_O$ both specialise to $x_n$. Then the two branch ideals — the preimages, under the specialisation maps on stalks, of the maximal ideals of the stalks at $\xi_\infty$ and at $\xi_0$ — have sum equal to the maximal ideal of the local ring of $X_O$ at $x_n$.
--
--   This is the transversality statement for the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$: at a crossing point of the two components of the special fibre the two local branches meet transversally, so their branch ideals already generate the maximal ideal. It is used to produce an explicit pair of germs generating the maximal ideal and thence oriented étale charts adapted to a crossing, via [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart).
